<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:windows">
<!--
    kuna re-quadratic-transform-loses-four: a stack buffer initialised by a run
    of direct frame stores and then walked by a pointer loop prints with its
    declaration and all of its reads, but with none of its initialisation.

    Heritage::guard ends with an arm upstream Ghidra runs whenever a pointer can
    reach the range being heritaged (heritage.cc:1194, gated on
    Architecture::highPtrPossible).  Heritage::guardLoads (heritage.cc:1570)
    puts an addrforce CPUI_COPY read of the range in front of every
    indexed-stack LOAD whose discovered guard range covers it, so a slot that is
    only ever READ through a computed pointer still has a reader where the
    pointer is dereferenced.  kuna shipped that arm behind a hard-coded
    highPtrPossible == false, so the slot had no reader at all and
    ActionDeadCode deleted the store.

    The vector is sub_401330 of decoder.exe from the sddecoder crackme
    (challenge 5ab77f5f33c5d40ad448c820), MSVC i386, 252 bytes at 0x401330.  It
    loads a 128-bit constant into the top four dwords of its own frame:

        401330  83 ec 20              SUB   ESP,0x20
        401333  a1 bc 60 40 00        MOV   EAX,[0x4060bc]
        401338  8b 0d c0 60 40 00     MOV   ECX,[0x4060c0]
        40133e  8b 15 c4 60 40 00     MOV   EDX,[0x4060c4]
        401344  89 44 24 10           MOV   [ESP+0x10],EAX
        401348  a1 c8 60 40 00        MOV   EAX,[0x4060c8]
        40134d  89 4c 24 14           MOV   [ESP+0x14],ECX
        401355  89 44 24 1c           MOV   [ESP+0x1c],EAX
        40135d  89 54 24 20           MOV   [ESP+0x20],EDX   ; two pushes deep

    and then reads it only through LEA EAX,[ESP+0x20] at 0x401399 (four pushes
    deep, so the same 0x10 slot), which the inner loop walks a dword at a time.
    The four constants live in .rdata at 0x4060bc.

    Stage: P3 heritage guarding, option indexaliasguard off|load|full.  Pass 1
    (off) pins the bug: the array is declared and XORed through the pointer,
    with no initialisation anywhere.  Pass 2 (load, the shipped default) pins
    the recovered stores.  The reads are identical across both passes, which is
    the point: only the missing writes move.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401330">

</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x4060bc" readonly="true">
7f1ef735f0a7a63aa542c6057c0fc300
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401330" name="transform"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option indexaliasguard off</com>
  <com>lo fu transform</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option indexaliasguard load</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="INDEXALIASGUARD #1: both passes recover the same four-word stack accumulator, so only its initialisation is in question" min="2" max="2">uint4 v[0-9]+ \[4\];</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="INDEXALIASGUARD #2: both passes XOR it through the walking pointer, so the reads never moved" min="2" max="2">\*v[0-9]+ = \*v[0-9]+ \^</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="INDEXALIASGUARD #3: both passes read the finished accumulator bit by bit" min="2" max="2">v[0-9]+\[v[0-9]+ &gt;&gt; 5\]</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="INDEXALIASGUARD #4: load, the MOV [ESP+0x10],EAX at 0x401344 reaches element 0 (off emits no initialisation at all)" min="1" max="1">v[0-9]+\[0\] = dat_4060bc;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="INDEXALIASGUARD #5: load, the MOV [ESP+0x14],ECX at 0x40134d reaches element 1" min="1" max="1">v[0-9]+\[1\] = dat_4060c0;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="INDEXALIASGUARD #6: load, the MOV [ESP+0x20],EDX at 0x40135d reaches element 2 across the two intervening pushes" min="1" max="1">v[0-9]+\[2\] = dat_4060c4;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="INDEXALIASGUARD #7: load, the MOV [ESP+0x1c],EAX at 0x401355 reaches element 3" min="1" max="1">v[0-9]+\[3\] = dat_4060c8;</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
